svn-fw-limited-entity-hierarchy: an object of a limited hierarchy is in that hierarchy for its tickets

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 2, version 185): TPMT_TK_CREATION "hierarchy |
the hierarchy containing *name*"; TPMT_TK_AUTH "hierarchy | hierarchy of the
object used to produce the ticket"; Part 1, "EvictControl of objects in
firmware-limited and SVN-limited hierarchies": "Objects in a firmware-limited
or SVN-limited hierarchy (including objects without
*firmwareLimited/svnLimited* SET)". An object created under a parent in a
firmware-limited or SVN-limited hierarchy (or a primary/external object of
one) is contained in that limited hierarchy, whose proof protects its tickets
(Part 1, "Enrollment of SVN-Limited Objects": the hierarchies protect "from
vulnerable firmware that has access to base hierarchy seeds and proof
values").

The reference's EntityGetHierarchy() identifies an object's hierarchy by its
ppsHierarchy/spsHierarchy/epsHierarchy attributes, which hold the base
hierarchy, so TPM2_Create's creation ticket and the TPM2_PolicySigned/
TPM2_PolicySecret auth tickets of such an object are made for the base
hierarchy with its proof (while TPM2_VerifySignature, via GetHierarchy(),
already uses the limited hierarchy). tpm-rs uses the object's limited
hierarchy for all of them; the patch makes EntityGetHierarchy() return it for
objects of limited hierarchies (every other object is unchanged).
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Entity.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Entity.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Entity.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Entity.c
@@ -502,7 +502,17 @@ EntityGetHierarchy(TPMI_DH_ENTITY handle  // IN :handle of entity
                 object = HandleToObject(handle);
                 VERIFY(object != NULL, FATAL_ERROR_ASSERT, TPM_RH_NULL);
 
-                if(object->attributes.ppsHierarchy)
+                // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT
+                // determinism): an object of a firmware-limited or SVN-limited
+                // hierarchy is contained in that hierarchy (TPM 2.0 Part 2,
+                // TPMT_TK_CREATION: "the hierarchy containing name"; TPMT_TK_AUTH:
+                // "hierarchy of the object used to produce the ticket").
+                if(HierarchyIsFirmwareLimited(object->hierarchy)
+                   || HierarchyIsSvnLimited(object->hierarchy))
+                {
+                    hierarchy = object->hierarchy;
+                }
+                else if(object->attributes.ppsHierarchy)
                 {
                     hierarchy = TPM_RH_PLATFORM;
                 }
